6. Authentication / session
src/lib/auth.ts: session cookie nsocks_session containing the raw numeric user id (not signed/tokenized), httpOnly, sameSite: lax, secure in production, 7-day expiry; getSessionUser() loads the user from DB and rejects banned/suspended.
Passwords: bcryptjs, cost 10 (hashPassword/verifyPassword).
Guarding: only src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx redirects unauthenticated users; individual API routes call getSessionUser() ad hoc. No middleware-level protection.
2FA is demo-grade: toggle-2fa stores a fixed secret JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP and accepts any 6-digit code; login only checks code length — no TOTP verification.
forgot-password returns a mockToken and, if newPassword is supplied, resets the password with no token/verification step.
7. Database / ORM
PostgreSQL via pg Pool + Drizzle ORM (drizzle-orm/node-postgres); singleton in src/db/index.ts (throws if DATABASE_URL unset).
Schema: src/db/schema.ts — 14 tables: users, proxy_plans, user_subscriptions, crypto_deposits (legacy), crypto_deposit_addresses, crypto_payment_intents, crypto_payment_transactions, transactions, proxy_nodes, api_keys, bandwidth_logs, proxy_listings, owned_proxies, support_tickets.
Two DDL sources coexist:
src/db/init.ts — raw CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS run at request time + dev-only seedDatabase().
drizzle.config.ts (dialect postgresql, schema ./src/db/schema.ts) for drizzle-kit.
Drift: schema.ts declares provider/transport_*/access_*/public_access_* columns on users, user_subscriptions, transactions, api_keys, proxy_listings, owned_proxies that init.ts does not create; conversely dashboard_support_tickets / dashboard_support_messages are created ad-hoc by raw pool.query in api/support/create/route.ts and exist in neither file.
Seed data (src/db/seed.ts): demo users user@nsocks.io / admin@nsocks.io with hardcoded demo passwords, plans, nodes, ~60 proxy listings.
